 ],
 "summary": "Three new question words: itsu (when?), nannichi (what day of the month?) and nangatsu (what month?). Months are number + gatsu; the first ten days of the month just have to be memorized, with hatsuka (20th), juuyokka (14th) and nijuuyokka (24th) as irregular exceptions — and 8 is double 4, so youka (8th) has the longer 'yo' than yokka (4th). Full dates go month first, then day (juunigatsu nijuuninichi). Deshita is the past tense of desu: kinou wa tsuitachi deshita. The particle wo (を) marks the object and is never replaced by o. New hiragana: や ゆ よ わ を ん."
